    "created_at": "2021-10-06T09:33:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-06T09:33:24Z",
    "body": "> Yes, these days I'd kind of prefer to invert the model. Especially after @domfarolino's work revamping link fetching to be more hookable, I think more likely we could define \"linked resource fetch setup steps\" for stylesheets, and keep it all centralized in HTML.\r\n\r\nI tend to agree. To make the CSS variant variable it would need to copy or import things from HTML such as \"potentail-CORS\" stuff which should have knowledge about `crossorigin` attributes of link elements - an HTML concern rather than CSS.",
